From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:19:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/57] backends: let virtual input devices pinch, swipe and
 flip the tablet mode switch

Add clutter_virtual_input_device_notify_touchpad_pinch(),
notify_touchpad_swipe() and notify_tablet_mode(), implemented by the
native backend. Pinches and swipes start at the pointer and go through
the same path as a real touchpad's, and the device that flips the
tablet mode switch counts as the seat's switch, so touch mode follows
it exactly as it follows a convertible's hinge. Programs that drive the
desktop, such as Kestrel's checks, can pinch and swipe over windows and
fold a computer into a tablet and back.

Upstream-Status: forwardable
